    <item>
      <title>微牛金融因反洗錢缺陷被責令支付US$420萬罰款</title>
      <link>https://www.discuss.com.hk/viewthread.php?tid=32340177</link>
      <category>關於我們</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Published on: 2026-11-06T12:50:41+0800&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;!-- google_ad_section_start --&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Webull's (BULL) Webull Financial subsidiary has been ordered to pay a fine of $4.2 million by the US Financial Industry Regulatory Authority for failing to implement programs for anti-money laundering and identity theft prevention, FINRA said Thursday.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
微牛（BULL）旗下的微牛金融子公司因未實施反洗錢和防範身份盜竊的措施，被美國金融業監管局處以420萬美元罰款，FINRA週四表示。&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
The company has agreed to certify remediation of the deficiencies in its anti-money laundering and identity theft prevention programs, and retain an independent consultant to address its best execution program, according to a statement.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
根據一份聲明，該公司已同意證明其反洗錢及身份盜竊防範計劃中的缺陷已得到整改，並聘請獨立顧問對其最佳執行計劃進行改進。&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
The company opened over 120,000 new customer accounts between January 2020 and September 2023, using third-party identity verification services "without forming a reasonable belief that it knew the true identity of those customers," FINRA said.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
FINRA表示，該公司在2020年1月至2023年9月期間，通過第三方身份驗證服務開設了超過12萬個新客戶帳戶，但「並未形成對其真實身份的合理認知」。&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
Webull also failed to investigate 473 unauthorized Automated Clearing House, or ACH, transfers of over $1.5 million from other financial institutions into Webull accounts, the organization said.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
